        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0706" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1946v04/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.P.(Gen)Doc.1.J.1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article 12</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-outside-research" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1946-10-15T23:59:59+01:00" notBefore="1946-07-29T00:00:00+01:00"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Replace the first sentence of Article 12 by the following text: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Italy hereby cedes to Greece in full sovereignty
                                the Dodecanese Islands, enumerated as follows:</hi></p>
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Astypalaia, Rhodes, Karchi</hi> [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Khalki?</hi>], <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Scarpanto</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Karpathos</hi>), <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Casos, Piscopi</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tilos</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Nisyros, Kalymnos, Leros,
                                Patmos, Lipsos, Symi, Cos and Castelrosso</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Megisti</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">and the
                                smaller islets which depend upon these islands</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">see map</hi>).”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>The above text is proposed to avoid any ambiguity as to the expression “Isles of
                    the Dodecanese” by naming them expressly, which is in accord with diplomatic
                    precedents concerning the said islands (see Art. 15 of the Treaty of
                    Lausanne).</p>
            </div>
